{"id":"st430-6","designation":"ST 430-6","title":"D-Cinema Operations — Auditorium Security Messages for Intra-Theater Communications","state":"active","suite":"430","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st430-6/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st430-6/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"The Auditorium Security Message (ASM) specification enables interoperable communication of securitycritical information (information necessary to ensure security of D-Cinema content) between devices over an intra-theater exhibition network. The specification uses Transport Layer Security (TLS) for authentication and confidentiality, and Key-Length-Value (KLV) coding for message encoding. It defines a protocol, a general purpose request-response message set and a specific message set for link encryption keying.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Glossary","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"Overview (Informative)","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"Message Security, RRP Structure and General Requirements","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 Message Security: Transport Layer Security (TLS)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 Message Structure: Key Length Value (KLV)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 General ASM Command Elements","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.4 General TLS and RRP Requirements for Auditorium Security Messages","page":7},{"level":1,"title":"General Purpose ASM Commands","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"7.1 BadRequest Response","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"BadRequest Response","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"7.2 GetTime","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"GetTime Request","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"GetTime Response","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"7.3 GetEventList","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"GetEventList Request","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"GetEventList Response","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"7.4 GetEventID","page":10},{